/* ============================================================================
   ToolAdda — Chemistry Tools
   Element dataset: all 118 confirmed chemical elements.

   Shared by every tool inside /chemistry-tools/, so keep it free of any
   UI concerns. Exposed as globals (classic script, no bundler needed).

   ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
   FIELD REFERENCE
   ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
   z          Atomic number (number of protons).
   symbol     IUPAC element symbol.
   name       IUPAC English name.
   mass       Standard atomic weight in unified atomic mass units (u),
              abridged. For elements with no stable isotope this is instead
              the mass number of the most stable / best-characterised isotope
              and `massNum: true` is set — the UI then renders it as [98].
   massText   Present only where the published value ends in a significant zero
              that a JavaScript number would drop (20.180 becomes 20.18).
              Display code prefers it over `mass`.
   category   One of the CATEGORY keys below.
   group      IUPAC group 1-18. `null` for the f-block (57-71, 89-103),
              which sits outside the numbered groups.
   period     1-7.
   block      s | p | d | f. The f-block here follows the common teaching
              convention: lanthanides (57-71) and actinides (89-103).
   state      State at 25 °C (298.15 K) and 100 kPa: solid | liquid | gas |
              unknown. "unknown" is used where the bulk element has never
              been produced in a weighable quantity, so no state has been
              measured (astatine and everything from fermium onward).
   en         Electronegativity, Pauling scale. null where no accepted value
              exists (most noble gases, several synthetic elements).
   config     Electron configuration in noble-gas shorthand. The full
              configuration is expanded from this at runtime, so it is
              stored exactly once. Configurations for Z >= 104 are predicted.
   ox         Commonly encountered oxidation states.
   mp, bp     Melting and boiling point in °C at standard pressure.
   density    Density. g/cm³ for solids and liquids at ~25 °C; g/L for gases
              at 0 °C and 101.325 kPa. Unit carried in `densityUnit`.
   radius     Calculated atomic radius in pm (Clementi et al.).
   ie         First ionisation energy in eV.
   ea         Electron affinity in kJ/mol. null where the anion is unbound
              or the value is not reliably established.
   year, by   Year of discovery / isolation and the person or team credited.
              year is null for elements known since antiquity.
   radioactive
              true when the element has NO stable isotope. That is the rule
              used throughout this tool: technetium (43), promethium (61) and
              every element from bismuth (83) upward — 38 elements in total.
              Elements such as potassium or carbon, which have radioactive
              isotopes but also stable ones, are NOT flagged.
   desc       Short original description.

   Any value that is genuinely unknown is `null` and is rendered as "N/A".
   No value in this file is estimated or invented to fill a gap.
   ============================================================================ */

